// The sdfcore package: the GPU-safe half of signed distance fields, shapes
// as functions from a point to its distance from the surface (negative
// inside), pure arithmetic on f32s and geomath's Vec3s. The sdf package is
// its CPU side (the horn, curves that hold lists, a function as a shape, the
// mesher), and re-exports every public name here, so a program that writes
// 'import sdf use *' sees both; code meant for the GPU imports this package
// alone. A program reaches it with 'import sdfcore', and gets:
//
// - Primitives (primitive.cone): 'sphere', 'box', 'roundBox', 'capsule',
//   'torus', 'cylinder', 'cone', 'roundCone', 'taperedCapsule' (the round
//   cone between any two points: a bone, a branch, a spike), 'triangle' (a
//   flat sheet, thickened into a membrane or a panel), 'membrane' (the
//   sheet stretched between two spars, bowed and scalloped), 'plane',
//   'ellipsoid'.
// - Operators on distances (operator.cone): 'union', 'subtract',
//   'intersect', their smooth forms 'smoothUnion', 'smoothSubtract',
//   'smoothIntersect' (Quilez's quadratic smooth minimum) and
//   'smoothUnionBlend' (with the material blend factor); 'onion', 'round',
//   'exclusive'.
// - Operators on the point (domain.cone): 'translate', 'rotate',
//   'scalePoint' with 'scaleDistance', 'Placement' (all three);
//   'mirrorX', 'mirrorY', 'mirrorZ', 'mirror'; 'repeat', 'repeatLimited';
//   'elongate'.
// - hg_sdf's fillets (fillet.cone, MIT): 'unionRound', 'intersectRound',
//   'subtractRound', 'unionChamfer', 'unionColumns', 'unionStairs',
//   'intersectStairs', 'subtractStairs', 'pipe', 'groove', 'tongue',
//   'engrave'.
// - Repetition along a curve (curve.cone): the Curve and Repeated traits,
//   'repeatAlong' (a shape repeated in the curve's rotation-minimizing
//   frames, the exact union of every copy), 'Arc' (a circular arc, with
//   'project' and 'cells'), and 'repeatAlongArc' with 'arcCellFrame', the
//   same union on an arc, its cells stepped round with no trigonometry.
// - The Shape trait (shape.cone), and 'gradient' and 'normal' by finite
//   differences, generic over any Shape.
// - Detail from noise (detail.cone): 'displace' (not a distance) and
//   'fbmDetail' (Quilez's fBm of spheres, a bound), with 'latticeSpheres'.
//
// Numbers are f32, points geomath's Vec3. A shape is written as code:
//
//   fn scene(p Vec3) f32 {
//     imm body = sphere(p, 1.);
//     imm hole = cylinder(rotate(p, turn), 2., 0.4);
//     smoothSubtract(body, hole, 0.1);
//   }
//
// EXACT AND BOUNDED. A distance is exact when it is the Euclidean distance
// to the surface, a bound when it never exceeds it (a sphere tracer stays
// safe, and a mesher finds the same surface). Each function's comment says
// which it gives; sdf's tests sample the gradient's length (at most 1 for
// either) for those that claim one.
//
// GPU-SAFE. Nothing here allocates, holds a list or an owning reference,
// makes a function or virtual reference, recurses, chooses a reference at
// run time, or uses a number wider or narrower than 32 bits; the generic
// functions (over Shape, Curve, Repeated) are copied for each shape, so no
// trait is ever reached through a virtual reference. So the package can be
// marked for the GPU once congo reads that marking, and the same source
// stays the CPU's. What still stands in the way of running it there: absf
// and floorf call the C library (scalar.cone), as does
// geomath's atan2, which 'Arc.project' calls; and geomath and noise, which
// it imports, are not themselves split or marked. 'Arc.make', 'frameAt'
// and 'cells' take sin and cos, and 'project' atan2, whose GPU results
// differ from the CPU's in the last bits (sdf's README, "CPU and GPU
// agree").
//
// sdf.slang, in the sdf package, holds these same functions for shaders
// (and sdf's horn), kept in step by hand and checked by sdf's parity test.
//
// Its files are one module, and only this one, the root, imports:
//
//   scalar.cone     helpers, Blend, CurveFrame
//   primitive.cone  the primitives
//   operator.cone   union, subtraction, intersection, smooth and hard; onion, round
//   domain.cone     translation, rotation, scale, mirrors, repetition, elongation
//   fillet.cone     hg_sdf's fillets (MIT)
//   curve.cone      Curve, Repeated, repeatAlong, Arc, ArcCells, repeatAlongArc
//   shape.cone      Shape, gradient, normal
//   detail.cone     displace, latticeSpheres, fbmDetail

mod sdfcore;

import libc;
import geomath use *;
import noise;
